# Line endings for a repository edited on both macOS and Windows.
#
# Text files are stored with LF in the repository and checked out with LF on every platform,
# whatever core.autocrlf says. Python, PowerShell 5.1+/7, and Inno Setup 6 all read LF files.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows build inputs. They were already LF before this file existed, and CI builds them as LF,
# so they follow the default rule above. Their encoding is not touched: setup.iss and
# ChineseSimplified.isl are UTF-8 without a BOM. Add "eol=crlf" here only if a tool proves to need it.
#   *.ps1  *.iss  *.isl

# Batch files are parsed line by line by cmd.exe, which misreads LF-only files in some cases
# (labels and GOTO). None exist yet; this keeps future ones safe.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary assets. Never convert or diff them as text.
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ttf binary
*.ttc binary
*.otf binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.pyd binary
*.zip binary

# Third-party license texts are kept byte-for-byte as shipped upstream, CRLF and mixed endings
# included. They are bundled with the installer and must not be rewritten.
source/licenses/** -text
